From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:50:24 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Add wlr-screencopy tests

Run a screencopy client against the test backend. It maps a fullscreen
window whose pixels encode their own coordinates and checks the
captures pixel by pixel:

- capture_output returns the whole output, unflipped, in the advertised
  XRGB8888 size and stride
- capture_output_region returns the region, clipped to the output; a
  region outside the output fails
- the first copy_with_damage completes at once with full damage; the
  next one waits for damage and reports the changed area
- a buffer of the wrong size is an invalid_buffer protocol error
- turning allow-screen-capture off fails frames in flight and hides the
  global from new registries; captures through an already bound manager
  fail; turning it back on restores both
- with allow-screen-capture off a new client is not offered the global

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
